# Response headers for the Cloudflare deployment.
#
# The same policy the Netlify config carried, in the `_headers` convention the
# static-assets layer reads — that config is gone, this file is the only copy.
# `script-src` stays
# 'self' with no 'unsafe-inline' — the site ships one same-origin script and
# registers the service worker from inside it, and Cloudflare injects no badge
# script of its own, so nothing needs an escape hatch.
#
# frame-ancestors names the Dashboard Portal: it shows this dashboard in a
# preview frame, and 'none' made the preview refuse to load. The portal is
# served from one host now — dashboards-home-portal.pages.dev, which its manifest
# and every link use; its workers.dev address used to be named here too, and the
# Workers are gone. The old *.netlify.app origin it used before is gone as well,
# and this is origin-scoped to the portal rather than `*`, so no other site can
# frame us.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self' https://dashboards-home-portal.pages.dev
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
